<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Plan 53 §7 B10. REMOVING A TAKE MUST RENUMBER THE COMP MAP AND DROP THE
  SEGMENTS THAT NAMED IT, AND UNDO MUST RESTORE THE WHOLE PREVIOUS MAP.

  Neither STakeStack::removeTake nor SRemoveTakeAction::apply referenced
  compMap_ at all. removeTake renumbers activeTake_ with exactly the arithmetic
  the map needs, three lines above where the map was ignored. So removing take 0
  of a comped column left every segment pointing ONE TAKE OFF, and a segment
  naming the removed take pointed at an index that no longer exists.

  WHY THREE TAKES AND NOT TWO. Plan 53 asks for a "comped two-take column", and
  that cannot gate this: invariant 3 COLLAPSES a single-take stack back to a
  plain cut, so removing one of two takes destroys the column and takes the map
  with it — the renumbering is never reached. Three takes leave two behind, the
  column survives, and the map has to be correct.

  THE MAP AND THE ACTIVE TAKE DISAGREE IN EVERY ASSERTED WINDOW. That is the
  rule comp_map_survives_split.qxa learned the hard way: an empty or ignored map
  means "ask activeTake_", so if they agreed a broken map would render identical
  audio and only the structural assertions would bite.

  THE TAKES, and why take 2 repeats take 0's slip:

      take 0  unslipped          window 4 = 0.4125   <- the one removed
      take 1  slipped 1 s        window 4 = 0.0  (the file's own silence)
      take 2  unslipped          window 4 = 0.4125

  Take 2 has to SURVIVE the removal and be audibly distinguishable from take 1,
  and two profiles are enough for that. Every number is from
  comp_map_audible.qxa's measurements of test_gapsaw.wav, not invented here.

  THE ARITHMETIC THE CASE PINS. Before: { 0 -> take 2 }, { 48000 -> take 0 },
  { 144000 -> take 1 }. Removing take 0 must DROP the middle segment (it names
  the departing take) and DECREMENT the others, giving

      { 0 -> take 1 },  { 144000 -> take 0 }

  Window 4 then reads take 0, which is the old take 1: the file's silence. With
  the map left UNRENUMBERED it would read its old take 1, which is now take 2's
  material: 0.4125, loud. So the audible half is silence-versus-loud, and the
  structural half catches the dropped segment, which no render can see because
  takes 0 and 1 agree over the span it covered.

  ON main THIS FAILS at the comp assertion after the removal and at window 4.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="remove_take_renumbers_comp">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <snap-to-grid-disable/>
    <add-track index="-1"/>

    <add-sample trackIndex="0" filePath="../test_gapsaw.wav" timePos="0"/>
    <add-take clip="0,0" filePath="../test_gapsaw.wav" startOffset="48000"/>
    <add-take clip="0,0" filePath="../test_gapsaw.wav" startOffset="0"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" shape="direct" takes="3"/>

    <!-- Active take 0, so the map and the fallback disagree. select-take
         clears the map, hence it comes before the segments. -->
    <select-take clip="0,0" take="0"/>
    <set-comp-segment clip="0,0" at="0" take="2"/>
    <set-comp-segment clip="0,0" at="48000" take="0"/>
    <set-comp-segment clip="0,0" at="144000" take="1"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" comp="0:2;48000:0;144000:1" activeTake="0"/>

    <!-- BASELINE: the map is in force. Window 4 is take 1's silence, not the
         active take's 0.4125. -->
    <render filename="rtrc_pre.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="rtrc_pre.wav" startFrame="144000"
                         frameCount="48000" minRms="0.0" maxRms="0.002"/>

    <!-- THE REMOVAL of take 0, which is also the active one. -->
    <remove-take clip="0,0" take="0"/>

    <!-- Two takes left, the column survives, and the map is renumbered with
         the departing take's own segment dropped. -->
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" shape="direct" takes="2"
                        comp="0:1;144000:0" activeTake="-1"/>

    <!-- Window 4 is still silence: it now names take 0, which is the old take
         1. Unrenumbered it would name the old take 1 as take 1, which is now
         take 2's unslipped material at 0.4125. -->
    <render filename="rtrc_removed.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="rtrc_removed.wav" startFrame="144000"
                         frameCount="48000" minRms="0.0" maxRms="0.002"/>
    <!-- and window 1 is the surviving unslipped take, not silence -->
    <assert-audio-energy filename="rtrc_removed.wav" startFrame="0"
                         frameCount="48000" minRms="0.0840" maxRms="0.0857"/>

    <!-- UNDO restores the WHOLE previous map, including the dropped segment,
         which is not re-derivable from the renumbered one: its position and
         xfade are gone. -->
    <undo count="1"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" shape="direct" takes="3"
                        comp="0:2;48000:0;144000:1" activeTake="0"/>
    <render filename="rtrc_undone.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4.0"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="rtrc_undone.wav" startFrame="144000"
                         frameCount="48000" minRms="0.0" maxRms="0.002"/>

    <!-- REDO removes it again, so neither direction is a one-shot. -->
    <redo count="1"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" takes="2" comp="0:1;144000:0"/>
  </actions>

</SActionScript>
